From 739fad9a1d7c47ad51a17f89081a46d0b7784495 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anthonybartczak <49080651+anthonybartczak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:02:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] Take only a notification or the service-open reply for a
 message

The realigner passed a candidate whose body began with any value that
decodes. A false header in front of a real notification, over a nil and
that notification, was passed on as a message and took the notification
with it, with nothing counted as skipped.

The device sends two things on this channel, and the 70 507 messages in
the HX Edit captures hold nothing else: a notification, and the bare
service number that answers the service opening. Either fills its
declared body exactly. A candidate is now one of those two or it is
stepped over.

For the same reason only a whole notification behind an unfinished
header shows that the header was false. The nine bytes of the
service-open reply can turn up as data inside a real notification, and
no longer count.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
